{"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/persistence\/segmentstore"]}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"anchor":"Stores","title":"Stores","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/RecordStore","doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/DropReport"]}],"metadata":{"role":"symbol","symbolKind":"struct","externalID":"s:11Persistence12SegmentStoreV","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SegmentStore","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"SegmentStore","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"SegmentStore","kind":"identifier"}],"remoteSource":{"fileName":"SegmentStore.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Traffluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Persistence\/SegmentStore.swift#L69"},"roleHeading":"Structure","modules":[{"name":"Persistence"}]},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"relationshipsSections":[{"type":"conformsTo","kind":"relationships","title":"Conforms To","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/RecordStore","doc:\/\/Persistence\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/Persistence\/s16SendableMetatypeP"]}],"abstract":[{"text":"A ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/RecordStore","type":"reference"},{"text":" that keeps records in a directory of append-only segment files, bounded in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"size, until they are delivered.","type":"text"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence"]]},"kind":"symbol","sections":[],"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Initializers","title":"Initializers","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/init(events:directory:byteBound:segmentByteCount:)"]},{"anchor":"Instance-Properties","title":"Instance Properties","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/byteCount","doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/directory","doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/dropReports","doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/pendingRecordCount"]},{"anchor":"Instance-Methods","title":"Instance Methods","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/append(_:)","doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/synchronize()","doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/takeRecoveredRecords()"]},{"anchor":"Type-Properties","title":"Type Properties","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/defaultByteBound","doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/defaultDirectory"]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"SegmentStore"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"overview","text":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["let store = try SegmentStore(events: [SignedUp.self, CheckedOut.self])","let tracker = Tracker(store: store)","let delivery = tracker.records.batch().deliver(to: vendor)"],"type":"codeListing"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Write-through.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" A tracker’s worker writes each record as it reaches it, before publishing"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it, with one "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"write()"},{"type":"text","text":", off the tracking caller’s thread, so the record survives the app"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"crashing or being killed from then on. The store makes the log durable against"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"power loss too ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"fsync"},{"type":"text","text":") once per batch, before the batch is delivered, and whenever"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/synchronize()"},{"type":"text","text":" is called: call it, after the tracker’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"flush()"},{"type":"text","text":", as the app moves to the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"background or terminates."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"A record whose write fails (the disk is full, say) is kept in memory only, and reported as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/DropReport\/writeFailed(recordCount:timestamps:)"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"What is kept.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" Only events of the types in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"events"},{"type":"text","text":", which conform to "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/BinaryCodable","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Events of any other type are kept in memory only: they are delivered in this run like any"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"other, are never written, and are lost if the app ends first. The first record of each such"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"type is reported as "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/DropReport\/notPersisted(event:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", so a type left out of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"events"},{"type":"text","text":" by"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"mistake shows up."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"A record’s context is not kept: a recovered record is in the top-level "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ServiceContext"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"as its span ended with the earlier run."}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Deleting.","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" A segment is deleted as a whole once every record in it is delivered, so a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"log whose records are all delivered holds no files. A segment kept for one undelivered","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"record keeps its delivered ones too. Only recovery rewrites a segment: one still holding","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"records after it drops some (","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/DropReport\/undecodable(recordCount:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/DropReport\/versionMismatch(event:storedVersion:currentVersion:recordCount:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":") is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"rewritten without them, so each drop is reported once. Should the rewrite fail, the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"segment is kept as it was and the next launch reports those drops again.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Reading back.","type":"text"}]},{"text":" When a destination’s full buffer drops a batch on its way through a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"delivery, the delivery reads that batch’s records back from the log once the destination","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"has caught up, reading each segment they are in once, and hands them to it in this run,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"each in the context it was tracked in, which the delivery keeps. A record the bound dropped","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"before the read finished isn’t read back, and one that can’t be read or decoded is logged","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and waits for a later launch.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Bound."}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" The log never holds more than ","type":"text"},{"code":"byteBound","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" bytes. When a record wouldn’t fit, the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"oldest segments are deleted until it does, and each one deleted with records not yet","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"delivered yields a ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/DropReport"},{"text":" on ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/dropReports"},{"text":". A record too large for an empty log","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is kept in memory only.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Recovery."}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" A store opened on a directory recovers the records earlier runs left there","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and a tracker given the store delivers them first. Each segment is cut at its first torn or","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"corrupt record, keeping every intact record before it, and the bytes cut off are reported.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"A segment comes back whole, delivered records and all. Each record a delivery had started on","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"comes back with ","type":"text"},{"code":"isRedelivered","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" set, as it may have reached a destination already: one","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"delivered before the app ended, or one delivered just as it ended, before the store could","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"delete its segment. A record whose delivery mark can’t be written is held back from that","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"delivery, so it is never sent twice unannounced, and delivered on a later launch.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Other versions."}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" A segment a newer release of the app wrote, in a later version of the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"format, is left on disk untouched after a rollback, for that release to deliver: this one"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"neither reads it nor counts it toward the bound. A segment in an earlier version, which this"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"one can’t read, is deleted and reported as a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/DropReport\/corruption(byteCount:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Changed event types."}]},{"type":"text","text":" Each record’s event is a map of its properties by name, so a record"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"written before its type changed still reads: a property removed since is skipped, an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"optional one added since is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"type":"text","text":" and one with a default value added since has it. A record"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"stored at another "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Event.schemaVersion"},{"type":"text","text":" than its type’s now is dropped without being read and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"reported as "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/DropReport\/versionMismatch(event:storedVersion:currentVersion:recordCount:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"One at the same version that can’t be read all the same, after a required property was added"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"or a property’s type changed without raising the version, is dropped and reported as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/DropReport\/undecodable(recordCount:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Open one store per directory at a time; two would delete each other’s segments. Copies of a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"store share its log.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"references":{"doc://Persistence/s8SendableP":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/s8SendableP","title":"Swift.Sendable","type":"unresolvable"},"doc://Persistence/documentation/Persistence/SegmentStore":{"title":"SegmentStore","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"SegmentStore"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/RecordStore","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" that keeps records in a directory of append-only segment files, bounded in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"size, until they are delivered."}],"role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"SegmentStore"}],"url":"\/documentation\/persistence\/segmentstore"},"doc://Persistence/documentation/Persistence/SegmentStore/directory":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/directory","title":"directory","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"directory"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:13SystemPackage8FilePathV","text":"FilePath"}],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Where the store keeps its segments.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/persistence\/segmentstore\/directory","type":"topic"},"doc://Persistence/documentation/Persistence/RecordStore":{"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"RecordStore"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/RecordStore","title":"RecordStore","url":"\/documentation\/persistence\/recordstore","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Where a tracker keeps each record until it is delivered, so records survive the app ending."}],"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"RecordStore"}]},"doc://Persistence/documentation/Persistence":{"kind":"symbol","title":"Persistence","url":"\/documentation\/persistence","role":"collection","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Keep each record on disk until it is delivered, so the records a tracker tracked survive the app ending."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence","type":"topic"},"doc://Persistence/documentation/Persistence/DropReport/undecodable(recordCount:)":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/DropReport\/undecodable(recordCount:)","fragments":[{"text":"case","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"undecodable","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"recordCount","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","text":"Int","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":")","kind":"text"}],"title":"DropReport.undecodable(recordCount:)","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/persistence\/dropreport\/undecodable(recordcount:)","abstract":[{"text":"Recovery read ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"recordCount"},{"text":" intact records it couldn’t decode: their event type isn’t in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the store’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"events"},{"text":", or its ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/BinaryCodable\/init(from:)"},{"text":" threw, as it does for a record","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"written before a required property was added or a property’s type changed while the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"event’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Event.schemaVersion"},{"text":" stayed the same.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol"},"doc://Persistence/documentation/Persistence/SegmentStore/synchronize()":{"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/synchronize()","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Flushes every segment written since the last flush to storage ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"fsync"},{"type":"text","text":"), so it survives"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"power loss."}],"title":"synchronize()","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"synchronize"},{"kind":"text","text":"()"}],"url":"\/documentation\/persistence\/segmentstore\/synchronize()","role":"symbol"},"doc://Persistence/documentation/Persistence/DropReport/notPersisted(event:)":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/DropReport\/notPersisted(event:)","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/persistence\/dropreport\/notpersisted(event:)","type":"topic","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"case"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"notPersisted"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"event"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"String"},{"kind":"text","text":")"}],"title":"DropReport.notPersisted(event:)","abstract":[{"text":"A record of the event named ","type":"text"},{"code":"event","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" was kept in memory only because its type isn’t one of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the store’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"events","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":": its records are delivered in this run, but never written, so they are","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"lost if the app ends first. Reported once per type, on its first record, for as long as the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"store lives; a type left out by mistake is added to ","type":"text"},{"code":"events","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},"doc://Persistence/documentation/Persistence/SegmentStore/dropReports":{"kind":"symbol","title":"dropReports","url":"\/documentation\/persistence\/segmentstore\/dropreports","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"A report of each drop, in the order they happen, from recovery onwards.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/dropReports","fragments":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"dropReports","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:ScS","text":"AsyncStream","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:11Persistence10DropReportO","text":"DropReport","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://Persistence/documentation/Persistence/SegmentStore/defaultDirectory"